# TwoSum by ordering: Fast2Sum of the operands ordered by magnitude with two selects. Unlike
# two_sum, its error term is finite whenever its sum is, so the sign of e can be trusted at the
# top of the range (decisions.md, the log of 2026-11-18).
kernel:        two_sum_ord
input:         a
input:         b
output:        r = s e
value:         a+b
status:        unverified
cone_exempt:   the operands are ordered by select; the IEEE-model statement says what s and e are for every operand

aa     = abs(a)
ab     = abs(b)
m      = lt(aa, ab)
h      = select(m, b, a)
l      = select(m, a, b)
(s, e) = fast_two_sum(h, l)
